  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania State University obligated $402M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Pennsylvania State University received 226 awards so far, with an average award size of $1.8M. Obligations were up 16.5% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $397M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market for Pennsylvania State University, with $399M in obligations. Smaller agency relationships and niche markets appear alongside the core DOD and R&D work: the Department of the Interior obligated $3M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2.4M, and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools accounted for $70.8K. A few NAICS categories and agencies show negligible or zero obligations. This snapshot reflects partial current-year totals and award-value nuances for largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, as noted in the summary.",
